package santa

// Authored eval vectors for sigma-rust's santa-probe-avltree-digest (fork PR 94, from its vector backlog, 2026-11-14).
// Measured first in santa.spike.AvlDigestProbe (local): the 220 selected rows and 26 controls, value and cost, as read.
//
// THE RULE, read in 6.0.7: `CAvlTree.updateDigest` copies its argument into the tree data UNREAD
// (CAvlTree.scala:31-34), and the reflective call asks only for a `Coll`, so a runtime tree can hold ANY collection
// as its digest: a `Coll[Int]`, a tuple constant (a `Coll[Any]`), a `Coll[(Int, Int)]`, bytes of any length. Only two
// things cast the digest to bytes: the AVL verifier's construction (CAvlTreeVerifier.scala:59) and the data writer
// (AvlTreeData.scala:75). Everything else works on such a tree:
//  * `.digest` hands the collection back (its runtime items, which is what these vectors' values are); keyLength,
//    the flags, valueLengthOpt, updateOperations, a later updateDigest do not read it; a modifying method whose flag
//    is off answers None first;
//  * `==`, `!=`, `indexOf`, `startsWith` compare the collections;
//  * `Global.serialize` of a tree with a BYTE digest of another length charges for the digest's own length (n - 33
//    more for n bytes): the cost rows;
//  * `substConstants` with such a tree as a new value at a position holding no constant never writes it;
//  * the lift (`Platform.liftToConstant`, Platform.scala:16-63) has no arm for a pair, an option or `Unit` as a new
//    value: such a call is refused, while a pair or an option INSIDE a collection is lifted with it (g11).
// An implementation that refuses a non-byte digest at updateDigest rejects scripts the JVM evaluates.
//
// The fixture is sigma-rust's: `tree` holds keys 1 and 2 (key length 1, flags 07), `T0` is it with every flag off.
// TWO FAMILIES: AvlTree.digest_any_collection_v6 (activated 3, tree v3) and AvlTree.digest_any_collection
// (activated 2, tree v0; the same outcomes, updateDigest being a v5 method). Every root is a property, a size, a
// comparison or `.digest` (sigma-rust selected no row whose root is the tree, which cannot be written).

import io.circe.Json
import scorex.util.encode.Base16

import sigma.serialization.SigmaSerializer

object AvlDigestText {
  val Read = "`updateDigest` copies its argument unread (CAvlTree.scala:31-34), so the tree holds this collection, " +
    "and this read never looks at the digest."
  val Hand = "`.digest` hands back the collection `updateDigest` was given, with its own runtime items."
  val Flag = "The flag is off, so the method answers None first, before the digest is read."
  val Write = "The writer casts the digest to bytes (AvlTreeData.scala:75) and charges for its OWN length."
  val Eq = "The comparer compares the two collections as they are."
  val Subst = "A position that holds no constant is not written, so the tree in the new value is never serialized."
  val Lift = "`substConstants` lifts its new values by class (Platform.liftToConstant, Platform.scala:16-63); the " +
    "table has no arm for a pair, an option or Unit."
}

